      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-24T15:27:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, on x86 a single 64-bit write is immediately visible to other CPUs, so this is only about preventing the compiler from reordering instructions, so that on the reader side `pkvm_initialized` is actually read from memory before it is used (see barrier() in the x86 implementation of __smp_load_acquire() I pasted above).",
      "parentUuid": "79e1c95e_f6cea7b5",
      "revId": "d3af314c3de63da776d34363949c57fb68b3fabc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
